## 🇬🇧 English Version: Privacy Policy & Data Protection

**Mr. Judger** is committed to upholding the highest standards of user privacy, data confidentiality, and secure AI-assisted legal arbitration. This policy explains how information is collected, processed, and protected.

### 1. Zero Unsolicited Data Retention
- **Voice & Claim Statements:** Audio recordings and written arguments from both parties (Plaintiff and Defendant) are processed strictly in real-time to transcribe audio and synthesize impartial legal arbitration decrees.
- **No Third-Party Sharing:** User dispute claims, evidentiary attachments, and transcripts are never sold, rented, or distributed to advertising networks or third parties.

### 2. Client-Side & Local Storage Architecture
- Case histories and past decrees are stored locally within the user's browser (**Local Storage**).
- Users retain absolute sovereignty over their data and may purge all records at any time using the "Clear Archive" option in the interface.

### 3. Payment Processing & Financial Security ($1 USD Pass)
- Single-pass PDF printing licenses ($1.00 USD) are handled through verified international payment gateways (PayPal / Credit Card networks).
- Mr. Judger does not store, process, or have access to sensitive card details (Card Numbers, Expiry Dates, CVVs).

### 4. AI Processing & Transmission Encryption
- All client-server communications use end-to-end industry standard encryption (**HTTPS / TLS**).
- Claim data submitted to AI reasoning pipelines is treated as confidential and is not utilized to train public machine learning datasets.

### 5. User Rights
- Full access to clear case histories at will.
- Anonymous case deliberation with no intrusive mandatory profiling.
- Immediate access to official decree outputs.

